  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;pressure, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>&nbsp;is volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is universal gas constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is temperature. The physical quantity equivalent&nbsp;to the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is:</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Pressure gradient",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Energy",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Impulse",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Coefficient of viscosity",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;have the same dimensions.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;also have the same dimensions.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>So, the dimensions of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>This is the dimensional form of energy. Hence, this is the right option.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}